From: anyfs-reader <noreply@anyfs.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] osdep: guard pthread_jit_write_protect_np() for macOS < 11

qemu_thread_jit_execute()/qemu_thread_jit_write() call
pthread_jit_write_protect_np() on every macOS build, but the function only
exists since macOS 11. A build for an older deployment target (anyfs-reader
targets macOS 10.13 on x86_64 and compiles with
-Werror=unguarded-availability, because the linker would otherwise turn the
call into a weak import that is NULL at run time) cannot compile osdep.h.
Older macOS runs only on Intel, which has no per-thread JIT write protection
to toggle, so skip the call there.

--- a/include/qemu/osdep.h	2026-10-09 18:18:17.682022184 +0800
+++ b/include/qemu/osdep.h	2026-10-09 18:18:17.690022245 +0800
@@ -839,14 +839,22 @@
  * for the current thread.
  */
 #ifdef __APPLE__
+/*
+ * pthread_jit_write_protect_np() is macOS 11+; older (x86_64 only) macOS
+ * has no per-thread JIT write protection to toggle.
+ */
 static inline void qemu_thread_jit_execute(void)
 {
-    pthread_jit_write_protect_np(true);
+    if (__builtin_available(macOS 11.0, *)) {
+        pthread_jit_write_protect_np(true);
+    }
 }
 
 static inline void qemu_thread_jit_write(void)
 {
-    pthread_jit_write_protect_np(false);
+    if (__builtin_available(macOS 11.0, *)) {
+        pthread_jit_write_protect_np(false);
+    }
 }
 #else
 static inline void qemu_thread_jit_write(void) {}
